.TH ZASH 1 "March 2026" "zash 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zash \- bash\-like interactive shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zash
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B zash \-c
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zash
is an interactive shell with a bash\-like grammar: conditionals, pipelines,
functions,
.BR alias ,
and a configurable
.B PS1
prompt. Builtins include
.BR echo ", " cd ", " pwd ", " export ", " alias ", " help ", and others.
.PP
With no options and no
.B \-c
argument,
.B zash
reads commands from standard input. When standard input is a terminal, it
prints an expanded prompt before each line (see
.BR PS1 " below)."
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c \ command
Run
.I command
as a single line, then exit with the command's status.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage message and exit successfully.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PS1
Prompt string. Supports backslash escapes such as
.BR \eu ,
.BR \eh ,
.BR \ew ,
.BR \eW ,
.BR \e$ ,
and others described in the inline
.B help
builtin.
.SH FILES
Installed bash\-completion definitions are typically in
.IR /usr/share/bash\-completion/completions/zash .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR sh (1)
.SH AUTHORS
The zash developers.
